## Part 2 — Parsing Pseudocode

```
function parseEventTitle(title):
  if title.startsWith("D#"):
    parts = splitByDelimiter(title.replace("D# ",""), " # ")
    return {
      type: "delivery",
      route: parts[0],
      driver: parts[1],
      destination: parts[2]
    }

  elif title.startsWith("P#"):
    parts = splitByDelimiter(title.replace("P# ",""), " # ")
    return {
      type: "production",
      lineName: parts[0],
      taskDetails: parts[1]
    }

  elif title.startsWith("A#"):
    match = regexMatch(title, "A# (.+) \((.+)\)")
    return {
      type: "attendance",
      employeeName: match[1],
      status: match[2]   // "Absent" or "Leave"
    }

  else:
    return null


function buildEventTitle(type, fields):
  switch(type):
    case "delivery":
      return `D# ${fields.route} # ${fields.driver} # ${fields.destination}`
    case "production":
      return `P# ${fields.lineName} # ${fields.taskDetails}`
    case "attendance":
      return `A# ${fields.employeeName} (${fields.status})`
```

